Q: How to create a conditional loop with Mono in Java? A: <p>I think you are looking for something like this:</p>
<pre><code>Flux.concat(
   // run at least once
   handleProofRequest(record, order),

   // just create an infinite flow, like a while loop
   Flux.range(0, Long.MAX_VALUE)
      // concurrency=1 just to make sure you don't do it multiple times in parallel
      .flatMap({ handleDelayedRoundNumber() }, 1)
      // here we check when to complete the processing, like in the while loop
      .takeUntil(roundNumber -&gt; roundNumber &lt; order.clientMetadata().timeout())
      // if the handler returns Empty then it basically loops again
      .flatMap { handleProofRequest(record, order) }
  ) 
   // stops once we've got an element; or nothing if completed because of the timeout
   .next()

   // and the code you have at the bottom
   .filter(pair -&gt; pair.second() != null)
   .map(pair -&gt; pair.second())
   .flatMap(proof -&gt; doStuffWithProof(proof));  
</code></pre>

Q: How to include a file only if the file exists in PHP? A: <p>Do not use file_exists().  file_exists() will return if the file exists, but you almost certainly want to know if the file can be included.  For this, use:</p>
<pre><code>if (is_file($file) &amp;&amp; is_readable($file)) {
    include($file);
}
</code></pre>
<p>This prevents you from trying to include directories and files whose permissions are such that they can not be included.</p>
<p>If you are paranoid, you can check the file first with:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>exec(&quot;php -l &quot; . escapeshellarg($file), $output, $return_var);
</code></pre>
<p>or if you're slightly less paranoid and want something much faster:</p>
<pre><code>$code = file_get_contents($file);
try {
    token_get_all($code, TOKEN_PARSE);
    include($file);
} catch (ParseError $e) {
    echo &quot;Syntax error in '{$file}': &quot; . $e-&gt;getMessage();
}
</code></pre>
<p>But of course, neither is a way to prevent malicious or buggy code from wreaking havoc, so be careful.</p>
